BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Access to Housing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261223T160000
UID:6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you seeking housing support or have questions about afford
 able housing options? Join us at S. Walter Stewart Library for personalize
 d\, one-on-one assistance with a Housing Services Worker.\nEast York Housi
 ng Help Hub is offering information session on the Rent Geared to Income o
 ptions available in\nMyAccesstoHousingTO\nonline system. Housing staff wil
 l support program participants with hands-on supports and help them comple
 te the registration process.\nFor more information or to register please c
 ontact East York Housing Help Hub at 416 698-9306 or email eyhhc@eyetfrp
 .ca.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c343bc7d3cd580062952e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board Games for Adults: Tuesday Evening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T200000
UID:6963ea5a94297d3600a495e4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the fun of playing modern and classic board games!
 \nDrop in with your friends (or make some new ones) and play games like:\n
 Anomia\, Backgammon\, Bananagrams\, Chess\, CodeNames\, Exploding Kitten
 s\, Monopoly\, Quirkle\, Rumikub\, Scrabble\, Sorry\, Set\, SushiGO\, UN
 O\, and many more!\nPlease don't hesitate to call us or visit the red des
 k on the first floor if you have any questions.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, E-Learning Lab on the 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6963ea5a94297d3600a495e4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Runnymede Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T193000
UID:6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbecd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion of Claire Keegan's\,\nSmall Th
 ings Like These\nIt is 1985\, in an Irish town. During the weeks leading u
 p to Christmas\, Bill Furlong\, a coal and timber merchant\, faces his bus
 iest season. As he does the rounds\, he feels the past rising up to meet h
 im - and encounters the complicit silences of a small community controlled
  by the Church.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbecd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
