BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sanko Speaks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T164500
UID:6aa2f9b53dd190003e7105a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the Afrocentric principle of Sankofa\, this free p
 rogram uses creative activities and guided discussion to explore how past 
 experiences can help us develop positive coping strategies for today. Adul
 ts of all backgrounds are welcome.\nThis program is in collaboration with
  TAIBU Community Health Centre.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa2f9b53dd190003e7105a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
