DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T190000
UID:6ac3ef73295b3b0033caa12d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Malvern’s Creative Writing Club runs twice a month. No writi
 ng experience needed.\nConnect with other writers\, get inspired\, and fol
 low writing prompts. We will write together\, share feedback\, and discuss
 . Sharing is encouraged but always optional!\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac3ef73295b3b0033caa12d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weston Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270116T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270116T110000
UID:6aee59dc96ec3a003adfe4a3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion of Freida McFadden's\nThe Cras
 h\n.\nThis snowbound thriller follows the heavily pregnant Tegan\, who cra
 shes her car and suffers a serious ankle injury during a harsh blizzard. S
 he is taken in by an older couple\, Hank and Polly\, only to discover thei
 r remote cabin is a deadly trap.\nDrop-In. No Registration Required.\nLigh
 t Refreshments Served.
LOCATION:Weston\, Youth Hub Area\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aee59dc96ec3a003adfe4a3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
