BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movie Screening: Wildcat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T200000
UID:6afb43886d7b4d002c6782f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's feature:\nWildcat\nDescription: In 1950\, Flanne
 ry O'Connor visits her mother in Georgia when she is diagnosed with lupus 
 at twenty-four years old. Struggling with the same disease that took her f
 ather's life when she was a child and desperate to make her mark as a grea
 t writer\, Flannery enters a crisis that will pitch her mind into a feveri
 sh exploration of her catholic belief\, causing the lines between reality\
 , imagination\, and faith to blur.\nThis film is rated PG. 103 minutes. Dr
 op in. All are welcome!
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Downstairs theatre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afb43886d7b4d002c6782f7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
