BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heroic Legacies: Flash Gordon\, Conan and The Spirit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T200000
UID:6b0886e307bf12004fd68470@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For the release of Scott Chantler’s new graphic novel\,\nFla
 sh Gordon: Two Worlds\n\, TCAF\, the Beguiling and the Merril Collection a
 re proud to present a panel discussion featuring Chantler\, J Bone (\nThe 
 Spirit\n) and Jim Zub (\nConan\n). With many graphic novels to their credi
 t\, our panelists have all brought classic pulp characters onto the curren
 t comics page.\nBooks will be available for sale by The Beguiling at the e
 vent.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Auditorium\, lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b0886e307bf12004fd68470
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Runnymede Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T150000
UID:6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbece@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion of Claire Keegan's\,\nSmall Th
 ings Like These\nIt is 1985\, in an Irish town. During the weeks leading u
 p to Christmas\, Bill Furlong\, a coal and timber merchant\, faces his bus
 iest season. As he does the rounds\, he feels the past rising up to meet h
 im - and encounters the complicit silences of a small community controlled
  by the Church.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aca8a4f035faf0033dbbece
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
