BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cold Cases Cracked: An Introduction to Investigative Genetic Genea
 logy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T193000
UID:6afb831932ce6d08d54b43fc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How are DNA and genealogical research helping to resolve decad
 es-old mysteries? This presentation introduces Investigative Genetic Genea
 logy (IGG) and explores its application within Canada to identify unknown 
 individuals and advance cold case investigations.\nPlease register for us 
 to gauge attendance expectations. Drop-ins welcome.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afb831932ce6d08d54b43fc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
