BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Classical String Music: The French Connection in the Age of Louis 
 XIV with violin and theorbo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6af0b4d1198b996a80aa84d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Louella Alatiit and Jonathan Stuchbery for an intimate co
 ncert exploring French Baroque music from the court of Louis XIV to the vi
 brant musical life of Paris.\nFeaturing works by Robert de Visée\, Jean-F
 éry Rebel\, Nicola Matteis\, Henry Eccles\, Jean-Marie Leclair and Angelo
  Michele Bartolotti\, the program traces the distinctive French style and 
 its encounter with the growing influence of Italian taste.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (1st floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af0b4d1198b996a80aa84d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
