BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dystopia Nonfiction Book Club: On Tyranny & On Freedom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T153000
UID:6afc794404009d003389198b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us each month to discuss issues in politics and society\,
  and explore how powerful forces are exploiting our world and dystopian im
 aginings are becoming present-day realities.\nJanuary's books are\nOn Tyra
 nny: Twenty Lessons From the Twentieth Century\nand\nOn Freedom\nby histor
 ian Timothy Snyder. Copies of the books are available in print\, eBook a
 nd eAudiobook format. Book club attendees are encouraged to read the book
  in advance of the meeting.\n"In\nOn Tyranny\n\,\nHolocaust historian Timo
 thy Snyder draws from the darkest hours of the twentieth century--the rise
  of Hitler and Stalin--to provide hope for the twenty-first. As he writes\
 , "Americans are no wiser than the Europeans who saw democracy yield to fa
 scism\, Nazism and communism. Our one advantage is that we might learn fro
 m their experience."\nIn\nOn Freedom\,\nSnyder argues that "we have lost 
 sight of what Freedom mean\, and this is leading us into crisis. Too many
  of us look at freedom as the absence of state power: We think we’re fre
 e if we can do and say as we please\, and protect ourselves from governmen
 t overreach. But true freedom isn’t so much freedom from as freedom to
 —the freedom to thrive\, to take risks for futures we choose by working 
 together. Freedom is the value that makes all other values possible."\nDro
 p in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afc794404009d003389198b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
