DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T200000
UID:6aaad7d9ca248a002916459b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nPresent and past TPL’s EIRs\, their respective
  participants\, and TPL staff are all invited to meet up and share their 
 entrepreneurial stories and resources. Join this session\, hosted by Entre
 preneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, to expand your perso
 nal network through the TPL Small Business community and share your sugge
 stions on ways to make TPL’s Small Business Programs and Services serve 
 you better!\nIn this session:\nCreate a strong small business community wi
 th members who are motivated to help and support one another on a regular 
 basis.\nHelp the library serve you better while reaching more of the busin
 ess community\; provide suggestions on what small businesses really want f
 rom the library.\nExplore the use of the “Entrepreneurs Suite” at the 
 North York Central Library.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo appl
 y for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Jean\, ple
 ase fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad7d9ca248a002916459b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
