BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Grocery Store\, a Library\, and the Struggle for Space: Black Co
 mmunity-Building in Toronto\, 1920s–1960
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270126T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270126T200000
UID:6aef8a71938566ae4f57d8c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:P\nresented in collaboration with the East York Historical Soc
 iety.\nJoin the January meeting of the East York Historical Society.  Lect
 ure will be presented by Dr. Melanie Knight\; TMU Professor of Sociology a
 nd Black Studies.  Dr. Knight will discuss the story of the Home Service A
 ssociation\, a Black community organization in Toronto whose roots trace b
 ack to 1918.  This little known history offers a compelling account of how
  communities in Toronto build spaces of belonging\, support and collective
  life.\nTuesday\, January 26 2027\, 6:30 – 8:00 PM\, Drop in.\n6:30 – 
 Refreshments\, Meet & Greet\n7:00 – Welcome & Remarks\n7:15 – Presenta
 tion\n8:00 – Wrap up
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aef8a71938566ae4f57d8c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
