BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61de4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61de4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T143000
UID:69b45639a2492930199a12f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Share your love of reading at our Wednesday and Thursday Book 
 Clubs! We discuss new books and old favourites in a friendly\, welcoming s
 etting. Ask staff for more details.\nApr 8 - The Women by Kristin Hannah\n
 May 13 - The Kiss Quotient by Helen Hoang\nJune 10 - James by Percival E
 verett\nJuly 8 - My Brilliant Friend by Elena Ferrante\nAug 12 - The Sound
  of Gravel by Ruth Wariner\nSept 9 - Chain-gang All-stars by Nana Kwame A
 djei-Brenyah\nOct 14 - Tomorrow and Tomorrow and Tomorrow by Gabrielle Zev
 in\nNov 11 - The Betrayal of Anne Frank by Rosemary Sullivan\nDec 9 - How 
 to Solve Your Own Murder by Kristen Perrin
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b45639a2492930199a12f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee and Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270120T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270120T150000
UID:6aca753c377296003a4b1824@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and informal discussion about 
 services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and le
 t us know what information and resources you would like to access at the l
 ibrary and in the community.\nEach month we will be joined by a different 
 community organization.\nIn January we will be joined by Ombudsman Toront
 o to discuss housing\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all partic
 ipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.
LOCATION:Spadina Road\, Centre of room at Canoe Table
