BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Shana Talebpour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T235959
UID:6af61ea80ad4ed003a02c2d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of December\, the works of artist Shana T
 alebpour are on display at\nNorthern District library\n.\nShana is a self-
 taught artist working mainly with oil on canvas. Her style is modern impre
 ssionism\, inspired by the great outdoors of Ontario lakes especially Lake
  Huron\, where she often kayaks and camps for days at a time.\n"Shana work
 s to recreate freshness and vitality of nature. She would like to invite t
 he viewers to step into the moment as though looking through a window into
  the living landscape."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\
 nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhib
 it their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect 
 the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighborhoods.\nThe exh
 ibit can be viewed during Northern District library's opening hours.\nFree
 . All are welcome.\nImage Credit: Shana Talebpour
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor Art Gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af61ea80ad4ed003a02c2d7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
