BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Our Infinite and Inevitable Ends: Author Talk with A.D. Sui
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T190000
UID:6ad28c0429c3d6003330705b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this exciting author talk A.D. Sui will discuss their upcom
 ing novel Our Infinite and Inevitable Ends\, a sapphic cli-fi thriller\, a
 s well as science fiction's role in today's rapidly politically and techno
 logically changing world. Question and answer period to follow.\nThis sapp
 hic cli-fi thriller is a love letter to hope in the bleakest of times\, co
 mbining the multiverse-bending drama of This Is How You Lose the Time War 
 with the cat-and-mouse chase of Killing Eve.\nOn a near-future Earth devas
 tated by climate change\, Dr. Cassandra Barlowe is right where she wants t
 o be: working on an island of floating trash in the middle of the Pacific 
 Ocean\, as far away from Dr. Yana Gulsvig as possible. Cas’s research on
  plastic-dissolving fungi is undervalued and underfunded\, thanks to the i
 nvention of deleria\, a drug that allows glimpses into different timelines
 . For the average user\, it’s a way to view lost loved ones or experienc
 e a different life\, but it also offers a glimpse into worlds where humani
 ty has solved its many global crises. Now\, most science funding is dedica
 ted to trawling these different timelines\, searching for a reality with t
 he solution to the climate devastation.\nBut when Yana — the world’s l
 eading expert on deleria and Cassandra’s ex-lover — is killed in a mys
 terious explosion in the hub of deleria research\, taking the hope of reve
 rsing climate change with her\, Cas is arrested on charges of domestic ter
 rorism. Cas must delve through timelines to piece together what happened\,
  while watching other versions of herself and Yana live out the life they 
 could have had — happier\, more in love. As brutal government agents clo
 se in and her addiction to deleria grows\, Cas has to make a choice: live 
 in the spiraling branches of reality\, seeking closure for Yana’s death 
 until the drug shatters her mind\, or live in the now\, even if that means
  embracing her own damaged self and fighting\, however hopelessly\, for he
 r own future and that of humanity.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (first floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad28c0429c3d6003330705b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T153000
UID:6af20293035faf0033e2720a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oin\na Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event 
 series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid em
 ail address\n.\nAttend all four sessions in person at\nForest Hill Branch 
 on December 4\, 11\, 18 from 1-3:30pm.\nRegistration is a two-step procedu
 re. First\, participants must complete their registration through this pag
 e. After this step\, library staff will follow up to request additional in
 formation in order to complete the registration.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af20293035faf0033e2720a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
