BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Funmilola Adessun
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T235959
UID:6b0088b7ec8cc5003a256369@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of December\, the works of artist Funmilo
 la Adessun will be on display at Mimico Public library.\nFunmilola Adessun
  is an architect and mixed-media artist\, creating as byAjike--her alias a
 nd ode to joy\, culture\, and storytelling. Her work is a growing legacy: 
 a celebration of memory\, meaning\, and what it feels like to belong. Insp
 ired by the opulence\, kinship\, and spirited community of her Nigerian cu
 lture\, Funmilola draws\, paints\, and sculpts with tactile techniques\, e
 nergetic colours\, and rich textures to express her perception of what hap
 piness means in our world.\nTheme: Root to Bloom Life is one big garden\, 
 and we are the Blossoms--Seeds popping\, Children budding\, Teens blooming
 \, Adults Flowering\, Ripening\, Striving\, Thriving--Then\, we return to 
 earth\, Regenerating\, Seeding\, Budding\, Blooming. We Blossom always\, w
 ith our heads held high.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space
 \nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhi
 bit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect
  the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighborhoods.\nThe ex
 hibit can be viewed during Mimico library's opening hours.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Mezzanine
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b0088b7ec8cc5003a256369
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: The Nature Isle': Return to the Commonwealth o
 f Dominica by Powys Dewhurst
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T235959
UID:6b08614ac225ba002c108b3d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of December\,\nThe Nature Isle': Return t
 o the Commonwealth of Dominica\nby artist Powys Dewhurst is on display at
  North York Central Library branch.\nAt age 10 in Barbados\, Powys grew in
 terest in world issues\, science\, movies\, geekdom\, and access for all. 
 He and a friend\, Matthew\, created a comic book library for kids his age.
  A former photojournalist\, his work ran in WIRED\, Toronto Star\, WHO/PAH
 O\, and LA Times. He has produced events at Toronto Reference Library\, Un
 iversity of Toronto\, and Hot Docs. His work\, held in TPL collections\, w
 as chosen to represent Canada at EXPO. He has mentored and advocated for s
 tudents in Canada\, Chicago\, Kenya.\n"In 2000\, I returned to Dominica to
  connect with my family roots. Alone\, with an old motorcycle\, manual cam
 eras\, and 35mm film\, I explored mountain villages\, rainforests\, and sl
 ept on black sand beaches. Dominica was an Eden with a population small en
 ough to fit in Rogers Stadium\, shifting from agriculture and fishing to c
 ruise tourism\, yet still strong and culturally resilient. I focused on th
 e people\, not scenery\, and felt colour would distract. These images have
 n't been exhibited in Canada".\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit
 s Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists 
 to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to 
 reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.
 \nThe exhibit can be viewed during North York Central Library open hours.\
 nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Powys Dewhurst\; Old Man Su
 nday
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor Gallery space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b08614ac225ba002c108b3d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
