BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Dancing Flowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T235959
UID:6ae63f065ea4c386b3ec1b19@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of November the works of artist Mary Garr
 one are on display at the Yorkville Branch in an exhibit titled Dancing F
 lowers.\nArtist biography:\nA Toronto-based artist from Australia. She has
  studied abstract expressionism for two years with the techniques of Nicho
 las Wilton and Jenny Nelson. A flower photographer for many years\, she c
 ontinues with this subject matter in her acrylic and oil painting.\nArtist
  statement:\nI love the challenge of translating emotion into paintings us
 ing gesture\, palette\, value\, shape and line. While each painting is an 
 exhausting number of decisions for me\, the artist\, the goal is ultimate
 ly to bring joy to the viewer. Applying the visual principle that "lines a
 ctivate\," this series is entitled "There's a party in the garden and the
  flowers are dancing\," with each piece conveying an unavoidably positive 
 sensibility with gestures that deliver that message.\nThis exhibit is par
 t of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides s
 pace for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city.
  These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city 
 and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Yorkville branc
 h open hours. Please check the\nYorkville\nbranch page before your visit
 \, and call ahead to ensure the room has not been booked for a program or 
 meeting.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Yorkville\, Art Gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae63f065ea4c386b3ec1b19
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
