BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HPV and Cancer: What Everyone Should Know and What We Can Prevent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T190000
UID:6afe10e115292a005cfc6f59@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Can HPV show up years after you were exposed? Does a positive 
 HPV test mean cancer? Can you still benefit from vaccination as an adult?\
 nJoin Dr. Amanda Selk\, obstetrician-gynaecologist at Women’s College Ho
 spital and Professor at the University of Toronto\, for an accessible conv
 ersation about HPV\, a common virus that can affect people of all genders.
  Discover how HPV can cause cancer - and how vaccination\, screening and t
 he treatment of precancer can prevent disease. Dr. Selk will explain what 
 has changed in Ontario and what it means for you and your family.\nWhat to
  Expect:\nUnderstanding HPV:\nHow it spreads\, how it can remain undetecta
 ble for years\, and why a positive test does not necessarily mean a recent
  infection\nThe Cancer Connection:\nHow HPV can lead to cervical and other
  cancers\, and why prevention matters for people of all genders\nScreening
  in Ontario:\nWhy HPV testing has replaced the Pap test for routine cervic
 al screening\, when to get screened\, and who should discuss anal screenin
 g\nVaccination at Different Ages:\nWhat we know about safety and effective
 ness\, why school-based vaccination matters\, and who may benefit as an ad
 ult\nThe presentation will be followed by time for questions and discussio
 n.\nAbout the Presenter:\nDr. Amanda Selk is an obstetrician-gynaecologist
  at Women’s College Hospital and a Professor at the University of Toront
 o. She leads the Colposcopy Program at Women’s College Hospital and spec
 ializes in HPV-related disease\, cervical cancer prevention and vulvar con
 ditions. She is a past president of the Society of Canadian Colposcopists 
 and serves on the board of the International Federation for Cancer Prevent
 ion and Colposcopy. An experienced clinician\, researcher and educator\, s
 he helps patients and the public make informed decisions about their healt
 h.\nAbout the Series\nBridging Minds: Health & Science Conversations is a 
 partnership between the Toronto Public Library and Women’s College Hospi
 tal. Through monthly discussions led by experts from across different clin
 ical areas and scientific disciplines\, this series provides attendees wit
 h the opportunity to engage directly with our topics and speakers and empo
 wers communities to navigate health and science topics confidently\, inspi
 ring a future of informed decision-making.\nLearn more:\nhttps://www.women
 scollegehospital.ca/bridging-minds/\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtua
 l Zoom event is free to join but registration is required. Once registered
 \, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link.\nWe can’t wait to see y
 ou there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afe10e115292a005cfc6f59
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
