BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to D&D for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T200000
UID:6b04613e6d7b4d002c68551d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all adventurers!\nCome heed the call and learn the bas
 ics of Dungeons & Dragons. Learn the ins and outs of one of the worlds mos
 t popular Tabletop Roleplaying Games.\nNo experience required\, this is an
  absolute beginner friendly event.\nNo need to bring characters or charact
 er sheets. Pre-generated characters will be provided.\nThis program is int
 ended for a mature audience.\nRegistration is required. Please register on
 line or by calling (416) 395-5980. Space is limited. Registration opens 3 
 weeks before program date.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Program Room - Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b04613e6d7b4d002c68551d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Data Visualization Part 2 – Tableau Public
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T153000
UID:6b032ec0d164f314d93d8294@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join this in-person program that introduces the Tableau Public
  platform to create and share data visualizations online. Participants wil
 l learn how to present data by creating simple charts and dashboards in Ta
 bleau Public. This workshop is for participants who want to develop basic 
 Data Visualization and Tableau skills.\nPre-requisites\n: Basic keyboardin
 g and mouse skills are required. Introduction to Data Visualization Part 1
  is recommended.\nA free Tableau Public account is required\n.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b032ec0d164f314d93d8294
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de S. Walter Stewart
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T200000
UID:6b05ea0bdf15b4003a43f6e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aimez-vous lire en français? Avez-vous envie de participer à
  des discussions autour des livres dans une ambiance conviviale et déten
 due?\nRejoignez notre club de lecture en français! Venez échanger vos po
 ints de vue\, analyser ce qui vous a marqué avec le regard d'autres lecte
 urs\, et faire de belles découvertes littéraires.\nOn se réunit le 11 j
 anvier pour découvrir\n«\nLa colère et l'envie\n» d'Alice Renard\n.\nL
 e livre sera disponible en prêt à la succursale S. Walter Stewart à pa
 rtir du 9 novembre. Également disponible en formats\nnumérique\n\,\naudi
 o numérique\n\, et en\ngrands caractères\n.\nSi vous voulez en savoir pl
 us sur nos clubs de lectures\, veuillez nous envoyer un courriel à\nprogr
 ammesenfrancais@tpl.ca\nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre français mais q
 ue vous avez plutôt un niveau débutant\, nous vous encourageons à déco
 uvrir nos\ncercles de conversation\n.\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automa
 tique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’interv
 enant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. V
 euillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à :\
 ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b05ea0bdf15b4003a43f6e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Layoffs vs. Terminations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T190000
UID:6b05f25c7c779d002c9218ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Samuel Michaels\, a Toronto lawyer with a background in e
 mployment and corporate law\, as he provides the legal processes that empl
 oyers must follow and legal recourse options that exist for employees. The
  session will be followed by a Q&A session.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b05f25c7c779d002c9218ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RSV and Flu: Prevention\, Symptoms and When to Seek Care
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T200000
UID:6b061b1b5ce6ca0041ec46d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Respiratory illnesses like respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) a
 nd influenza (the flu) are common\, but knowing how to protect yourself an
 d your family\, recognize symptoms\, and decide when to seek medical care 
 isn't always straightforward.\nJoin Ilham Elias\, Primary Care Nurse Pract
 itioner with St. Joseph’s Health Centre and Urban Family Health Team\, f
 or an informative session on preventing RSV and the flu\, understanding va
 ccination eligibility\, and recognizing when symptoms may require medical 
 attention.\nWhat to Expect\nUnderstanding RSV and Flu:\nLearn about these 
      respiratory illnesses and why prevention matters.\nPrevention and Vac
 cination:\nExplore ways to      reduce the risk of RSV and flu\, including
  who may be eligible for      vaccination.\nRecognizing Symptoms:\nLearn h
 ow to distinguish      between common\, expected symptoms and warning sign
 s that may indicate a      more serious illness.\nKnowing When to Seek Car
 e:\nUnderstand when      symptoms may require medical attention and how to
  access appropriate care.\nAbout the Presenter\nIlham is a Primary Health 
 Care Nurse Practitioner at Unity Health Toronto\, with a background in pri
 mary care\, public health and multi-organ transplant\, as well as clinical
  training in infectious diseases. Her areas of interest include health pro
 motion\, disease prevention and empowering individuals and communities to 
 make informed decisions about their health.\nThis program is presented by 
 Toronto Public Library in collaboration with the West Toronto Ontario Heal
 th Team (OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social service provi
 ders working together to improve the health and well-being of communities 
 in West Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Pub
 lic Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted he
 alth programs and resources to help people make informed decisions about t
 heir health. Learn more by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\
 nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to join but reg
 istration is required. Once registered\, you’ll receive an email with th
 e Zoom link.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b061b1b5ce6ca0041ec46d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T113000
UID:6af7272e0ad4ed003a02e819@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What materials and processes existed before Adobe Photoshop? J
 oin us for a hands-on analog image making workshop to create a Cyanotype. 
 The Cyanotype is a photographic printing technique sensitive to a limited 
 near ultraviolet and blue light spectrum. It involves layering objects and
  transparencies. All are welcome!\nWe will supply all materials\, but feel
  free to bring an object or 2D silhouette for a contact print.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (first floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af7272e0ad4ed003a02e819
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
