BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nia Circle of Care
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T150000
UID:6abbfb40901b02002cbec7c4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free group program that supports mental wellness through gui
 ded discussion\, peer connection\, and culturally responsive approaches to
  healing. Led by trained facilitators\, participants explore strategies fo
 r managing complex mental health challenges in a safe and supportive envir
 onment.\nFree registration is required\, speak to library staff for assist
 ance.\nThis program is in collaboration with TAIBU Community Health Centre
 .
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abbfb40901b02002cbec7c4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: Diabetes Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T113000
UID:6b09a7b4821b6e002c0c9f00@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The West Toronto Diabetes Education Program provides free diab
 etes education and support for individuals living with Type 2 diabetes\, 
 prediabetes\, or at risk of developing Type 2 diabetes. In this workshop\
 , we will explore effective ways to prevent and manage Type 2 diabetes th
 rough healthy eating\, physical activity\, and lifestyle changes. Particip
 ants will gain practical tips and strategies to support their overall hea
 lth and well-being. All welcome!\nFree Workshop in English and Mandarin.\n
 In partnership with Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, Cultur
 eLink Settlement & Community Services & Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b09a7b4821b6e002c0c9f00
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
